WEBVTT

00:11.220 --> 00:17.330
Well, ladies and gentlemen, thank 
you for joining our kimodameshi!

01:50.020 --> 01:52.240
I'll explain the rules.

01:52.620 --> 01:57.600
You'll be touring the seven locations across 
campus known for their scary stories.

01:57.970 --> 02:01.290
The old tree of hangings, the 
garden of the eternally lost,

02:01.290 --> 02:05.800
the window into the netherworld, the hall 
of the head seeker, the impostor's mirror,

02:05.800 --> 02:09.260
the room of lingering voices, 
and the twisted observatory...

02:06.800 --> 02:08.030
Where's Rian?

02:08.030 --> 02:09.040
Dunno.

02:09.260 --> 02:12.470
I've indicated the routes on the 
print-out I'm about to hand out.

02:09.540 --> 02:11.300
Sorry I'm late.

02:12.470 --> 02:16.940
To finish, you'll be pairing up to 
visit each site and receive a stamp.

02:17.400 --> 02:20.290
Finally, we'll watch a horror 
movie at the observatory.

02:20.690 --> 02:24.570
Also, I haven't told the teachers 
about tonight, so don't get caught.

02:24.570 --> 02:26.200
Yeah, yeah.

02:26.200 --> 02:27.610
It'll suck if they find out.

02:27.610 --> 02:28.690
They won't.

02:30.480 --> 02:32.660
All right, let's start pairing up.

02:32.950 --> 02:35.410
So, in total, there are...

02:35.410 --> 02:36.540
Hey!

02:38.100 --> 02:39.530
Jasmine?

02:39.530 --> 02:44.390
How could you leave me out of all this fun?

02:44.390 --> 02:46.570
Weren't you sleeping?

02:46.570 --> 02:48.570
I'm feeling a little better now.

02:50.250 --> 02:52.820
Just don't push yourself too much, Jasmine.

02:52.820 --> 02:54.480
I know.

02:55.210 --> 02:57.370
Well, let's get started, then.

03:05.030 --> 03:07.080
One, two...

03:25.460 --> 03:26.680
So...

03:26.680 --> 03:28.260
First up...

03:29.240 --> 03:31.070
Thirty-two years ago,

03:31.070 --> 03:35.430
this is the tree where a student with scratches 
all over supposedly hung themselves.

03:35.430 --> 03:38.100
Did that really happen?

03:38.100 --> 03:40.150
Kinda sounds made-up to me.

03:40.150 --> 03:41.570
I wonder.

03:52.050 --> 03:56.310
I didn't think of you as the type to 
join these kinds of things, Lucy.

03:56.890 --> 03:59.250
Chise invited me.

03:59.250 --> 04:00.120
Chise?

04:01.540 --> 04:05.830
I'd feel guilty turning her down 
when she asks so hesitantly.

04:08.030 --> 04:09.710
S-So then...

04:10.220 --> 04:12.780
Why did you offer to switch pairs earlier?

04:13.060 --> 04:16.220
What are you going to do if
your snakes suddenly appear?

04:17.610 --> 04:18.880
Besides...

04:18.880 --> 04:22.280
I don't want to bother trying to talk 
to anyone except you guys.

04:23.960 --> 04:25.250
I see.

04:32.270 --> 04:33.500
Let's see...

04:33.500 --> 04:38.750
The hall where the man who'd lost his head 
during a sorcery experiment was last seen.

04:44.410 --> 04:47.160
<i>I haven't felt like this in a while.</i>

04:47.730 --> 04:49.920
<i>But it might be an opportunity.</i>

04:53.530 --> 04:55.350
Could you press the stamp?

04:56.220 --> 04:57.270
Okay.

05:08.320 --> 05:12.040
You're pretty meek, aren't you? Shy, maybe.

05:13.100 --> 05:15.990
You look like you want to talk 
to people, but you can't.

05:17.640 --> 05:20.290
I'm not good at talking to people.

05:20.290 --> 05:22.910
It just takes practice.

05:22.910 --> 05:25.750
You have no trouble talking to 
Rian and the others, after all.

05:27.100 --> 05:29.240
In that case, did you know

05:29.240 --> 05:34.380
that Philomela's being told to drop out 
of school due to her family's circumstances?

05:35.730 --> 05:38.010
So that's what you wanted to ask, huh?

05:38.010 --> 05:40.190
You're not very good at segues yet.

05:42.580 --> 05:44.430
Of course I know.

05:45.050 --> 05:46.610
But there's nothing to do about it.

05:47.140 --> 05:53.870
I heard the Sergeant family serves 
the Rickenbacker family... your family.

05:53.870 --> 05:58.870
So, you think I could order them 
to do something about it?

06:00.750 --> 06:07.100
Chise, dear mage, are your kind 
ever tied down by something?

06:07.640 --> 06:09.170
Tied down?

06:09.560 --> 06:15.350
A sorcerer's descendants are bound 
to their family from birth.

06:16.320 --> 06:19.420
No matter how much
 the world extols freedom,

06:19.420 --> 06:22.320
subjection exists in the shadows.

06:24.090 --> 06:30.240
Stick your nose into such places, and you'll 
find yourself in a lot of hurt, Chise.

06:33.710 --> 06:39.080
I've experienced the pain of stepping 
into someone else's core, too.

06:42.130 --> 06:44.890
You like Philomela, huh?

06:44.890 --> 06:45.560
Eh?

06:46.310 --> 06:48.120
Er, yeah.

06:48.120 --> 06:50.630
I'm worried about her.

06:51.600 --> 06:52.630
I see.

06:53.070 --> 06:55.630
Why don't we keep talking as we walk?

06:58.600 --> 07:02.960
She seems to have finally 
found friends, too.

07:09.110 --> 07:10.590
Miss Veronica!

07:10.590 --> 07:11.380
Poison?

07:11.380 --> 07:12.790
No... A curse?

07:12.790 --> 07:13.670
Take her away.

07:13.670 --> 07:14.940
This may be contagious.

07:18.920 --> 07:21.050
Miss Veronica, this way, quickly!

07:28.080 --> 07:32.280
<i>Poor girl. And on her first job, too.</i>

07:32.960 --> 07:36.590
<i>But to think someone would try 
to poison me on my birthday...</i>

07:38.840 --> 07:42.320
<i>I must really have people's attention.</i>

07:46.410 --> 07:51.620
They are all capable, close in 
age, and resistant to poison.

07:51.620 --> 07:54.150
I believe they're adequate 
to have by your side.

07:54.150 --> 07:57.000
What should I do with my father?

07:57.000 --> 07:59.740
He never discusses these things with me.

07:59.740 --> 08:04.730
The master insisted that we find someone 
immediately, given the recent incident.

08:07.640 --> 08:09.370
She survived.

08:09.370 --> 08:10.870
She's strong.

08:10.870 --> 08:13.680
That one's not mature yet.

08:13.680 --> 08:15.390
It was such a basic poison—

08:14.550 --> 08:16.030
I choose her.

08:17.220 --> 08:20.480
It'll be easier to talk to a girl.

08:21.360 --> 08:22.840
Miss Veronica!

08:22.840 --> 08:23.820
That's...

08:25.460 --> 08:27.360
Lizbeth Sergeant.

08:28.410 --> 08:30.610
This isn't a request.

08:33.230 --> 08:35.260
As you wish.

08:42.270 --> 08:43.740
Miss Veronica.

08:44.320 --> 08:46.180
Did Lizbeth do that to you?

08:48.300 --> 08:53.230
For not noticing the poison before I ate it.

08:53.760 --> 08:54.880
So...

08:55.400 --> 08:58.820
I'm sorry you have to see this.

08:59.340 --> 09:01.840
You're in a cage, too, aren't you?

09:02.370 --> 09:03.300
A cage?

09:03.300 --> 09:04.470
That's right.

09:04.470 --> 09:07.050
I'm still stuck inside, too.

09:07.450 --> 09:08.320
But...

09:09.390 --> 09:13.730
If you can't escape your cage, it may
 as well be a nicer cage, right?

09:15.760 --> 09:18.040
Which is why I'm choosing you.

09:19.210 --> 09:21.120
What's your name?

09:22.660 --> 09:24.360
Philomela.

09:24.760 --> 09:28.750
I'd like you to be my attendant, Philomela.

09:31.200 --> 09:34.610
But I'm a failure.

09:34.610 --> 09:36.500
Someone else could do better.

09:38.480 --> 09:40.260
Listen, Philomela.

09:40.970 --> 09:45.140
This isn't a request. It's an order.

09:48.050 --> 09:50.720
I understand.

09:50.720 --> 09:53.150
That's it. Good girl.

10:00.340 --> 10:04.610
To tell you the truth, I'm used to poison,

10:04.610 --> 10:07.170
but there are a few I'm still 
developing a tolerance to.

10:07.170 --> 10:08.890
So I'll need your help in the meantime.

10:09.840 --> 10:10.710
Yes.

10:11.130 --> 10:14.270
The Rickenbackers are a medical family.

10:14.270 --> 10:17.960
And yet, we're killing other members of 
our family, even. It's all so tedious.

10:18.760 --> 10:21.260
Do you have any siblings?

10:21.260 --> 10:22.610
No.

10:22.610 --> 10:24.960
Just my father's familiar.

10:25.400 --> 10:27.900
What about your father and mother?

10:28.280 --> 10:29.840
I don't remember.

10:30.490 --> 10:33.890
I heard they did something awful and died.

10:34.620 --> 10:35.500
I see.

10:37.910 --> 10:39.480
There. All done.

10:50.290 --> 10:52.300
Awful, isn't it?

10:52.300 --> 10:55.500
Everyone besides her is a villain.

10:55.500 --> 10:57.380
What a horrible bedtime story, isn't it?

10:59.060 --> 11:01.340
<i>I don't sense she's lying.</i>

11:02.500 --> 11:05.500
So, what are you trying to accomplish?

11:07.010 --> 11:11.970
I'm her master. What would you do in my shoes?

11:13.280 --> 11:16.440
If there's anything she wishes for...

11:16.440 --> 11:21.010
Even though she doesn't even 
know what she wants herself?

11:21.660 --> 11:22.880
Well...

11:24.220 --> 11:26.960
I'll ask again, Chise Hatori.

11:28.650 --> 11:33.600
You have no connection to this tiny little 
world where this is all happening.

11:33.600 --> 11:37.410
Why are you so insistent on 
involving yourself with her?

11:45.670 --> 11:47.020
You're adorable.

11:52.390 --> 11:54.570
Well, let's hurry.

11:54.570 --> 11:56.080
The others will catch up to us.

11:56.810 --> 11:58.330
Oh, yeah.

12:02.400 --> 12:06.900
This is the mirror that takes on 
your form when you answer its call.

12:09.610 --> 12:11.690
You sure are boring.

12:11.690 --> 12:13.910
What, are you still upset?

12:14.400 --> 12:18.990
I was just thinking about 
why you stopped me.

12:19.690 --> 12:20.510
No!

12:21.090 --> 12:25.010
I was doing you a favor by holding you 
back from charging in like an idiot.

12:25.010 --> 12:26.190
What do you mean, idiot?

12:27.010 --> 12:29.340
Can you really say that 
after what you did?

12:32.690 --> 12:34.900
I can't believe you're 
the heir to your house.

12:34.900 --> 12:37.480
I wouldn't want Jasmine working with you.

12:37.480 --> 12:38.910
I told you, I'm not...

12:38.910 --> 12:42.730
Wait, I thought you were taking
 over the St. George house.

12:42.730 --> 12:44.350
I dunno...

12:44.350 --> 12:48.100
The old folks keep nagging me to take over.

12:48.100 --> 12:51.610
But y'know how I like 
dressing up as a woman?

12:51.880 --> 12:52.760
Yeah.

12:52.760 --> 12:54.540
I'm sure that would be useful for sorcery.

12:54.540 --> 12:56.120
That's the thing!

12:56.530 --> 13:01.120
You know how cross-dressing is useful 
for special kinds of sorcery?

13:01.480 --> 13:06.630
The thing is, I only do it because I want to.
 I don't care about what my family has to say.

13:07.400 --> 13:11.700
But then my family started getting all up in 
Jasmine's business, since she's so proper.

13:13.200 --> 13:16.010
She cut her long hair short.

13:16.570 --> 13:19.220
Even started behaving more like a guy.

13:21.020 --> 13:23.500
Like she's trying to trade places with me.

13:25.590 --> 13:30.640
Some kids are just too honest to 
get themselves out of trouble.

13:30.640 --> 13:32.360
That's never occurred to you, has it?

13:33.370 --> 13:35.870
Are you talking about Isaac and Philomela?

13:38.620 --> 13:42.550
Rian, no bird is born knowing how to fly.

13:43.120 --> 13:46.380
They have to be taught by 
the one protecting them.

13:47.170 --> 13:50.980
But there are some humans 
who are never taught, either.

13:50.980 --> 13:54.370
Worse, some have their wings pulled 
out and buried under rocks.

13:55.080 --> 14:01.520
Hardly any hatchlings have the luck or 
the strength to leave such a nest.

14:04.290 --> 14:08.310
Unlike you, who was taught 
everything and granted everything.

14:12.720 --> 14:16.100
You're in the same position I am.

14:16.100 --> 14:18.120
And yet you've thought about it this much.

14:18.120 --> 14:20.720
You just aren't thinking <i>enough</i>!

14:20.720 --> 14:23.770
Isaac deserves an award 
for taking care of you!

14:25.030 --> 14:25.760
Okay.

14:25.760 --> 14:27.200
I'm done talking.

14:27.200 --> 14:28.520
And collecting stamps.

14:30.360 --> 14:33.930
<i>What exactly do I hope will happen?</i>

14:36.340 --> 14:37.400
Rian.

14:41.800 --> 14:42.770
Rian.

14:44.620 --> 14:45.100
Philo—

14:45.100 --> 14:45.930
Rian.

14:49.770 --> 14:51.350
What was that for?!

14:52.110 --> 14:54.660
Oh, it's just Kevin and the others.

15:07.710 --> 15:08.910
It's this window.

15:11.050 --> 15:15.020
Supposedly, those who look through it 
sometimes see their own final moments.

15:15.020 --> 15:16.720
I wonder if it's true.

15:18.560 --> 15:19.880
I don't see anything. Do you?

15:20.780 --> 15:23.810
It would be bad if you could.

15:24.630 --> 15:25.890
You're right.

15:32.180 --> 15:35.320
You can always bail if you 
don't feel up to this.

15:35.740 --> 15:38.030
I'll let them know at the goal.

15:40.350 --> 15:44.670
You've been sticking up for me lately.

15:45.310 --> 15:46.180
Why?

15:47.270 --> 15:49.080
Are you getting something out of it?

15:52.330 --> 15:58.220
It seems like Rian—or rather, all kinds 
of things—make you feel inferior.

15:58.220 --> 16:01.020
I'm the same way, so I just 
can't stand by and watch.

16:02.230 --> 16:04.490
You're Rian's friend.

16:04.900 --> 16:07.810
And aren't the Farrars the blacksmiths

16:07.810 --> 16:12.090
that the Scrimgeour family's been 
depending on for generations?

16:13.670 --> 16:18.420
At the very least, you aren't 
shadows like the Sergeants.

16:19.480 --> 16:22.790
Growing up with guy friends gets messy.

16:23.320 --> 16:25.670
We end up competing, even if we 
don't mean to hurt each other.

16:26.330 --> 16:29.640
And I have this habit of 
learning only after I mess up.

16:30.390 --> 16:33.120
I could never keep up with Rian.

16:33.840 --> 16:39.600
Like, when I get depressed or distracted, 
I can't focus on the family business.

16:43.030 --> 16:47.770
We work with fire, so the slightest 
negligence can cause a horrible accident.

16:48.490 --> 16:52.770
I have just a little experience with the 
kinds of things you've said to me, too.

16:56.340 --> 16:59.370
Rian thinks he isn't very talented.

16:59.920 --> 17:03.390
He thinks anything he can 
do, anyone else can do, too.

17:03.920 --> 17:09.530
He doesn't know what it's like not being 
capable... what it's like being stuck.

17:10.030 --> 17:11.410
Don't you think so?

17:12.090 --> 17:14.270
I do.

17:14.270 --> 17:15.250
Right?

17:15.250 --> 17:17.670
I think you might be the best 
person to tell him that.

17:18.330 --> 17:19.470
Don't you...

17:20.030 --> 17:22.160
Don't you ever tell him?

17:22.570 --> 17:27.270
How can you be around him
 after all you've been through?

17:28.360 --> 17:31.640
I'm not his rival or anything.

17:31.640 --> 17:34.190
So nothing I say to him sticks.

17:34.720 --> 17:35.560
But...

17:38.670 --> 17:42.090
But he's a good guy, so I can't 
bring myself to hate him.

17:42.760 --> 17:44.650
Maybe that's why I hang around.

17:46.060 --> 17:46.980
Yeah.

17:48.260 --> 17:49.620
He's straightforward.

17:50.020 --> 17:52.540
He isn't good at thinking 
deeply about people.

17:54.890 --> 17:56.060
I can't stand it.

18:00.660 --> 18:03.570
Well, it looks like we're headed 
to an upper floor next.

18:07.160 --> 18:08.640
<i>Tied down.</i>

18:08.640 --> 18:10.540
<i>By the outer world.</i>

18:10.540 --> 18:11.580
<i>By herself.</i>

18:12.760 --> 18:14.760
<i>Unable to move.</i>

18:14.760 --> 18:16.150
<i>Suffocated.</i>

18:16.720 --> 18:17.660
<i>Which is why...</i>

18:18.800 --> 18:20.170
Hey, Philomela...

18:22.090 --> 18:24.610
We'll go crazy if we don't vent sometimes.

18:25.100 --> 18:26.340
Both of us.

18:28.840 --> 18:33.940
<i>There are a few more things we need
 in order to move forward.</i>

18:37.110 --> 18:40.010
This is the last spot. The observatory.

18:45.170 --> 18:46.510
The stars.

18:46.510 --> 18:48.600
It's something like a planetarium.

18:51.570 --> 18:54.830
Martin, what's the movie we're watching?

18:54.830 --> 18:56.860
A brand-new movie from this year!

18:56.860 --> 18:59.790
An avalanche of sharks, attacking 
on a snowy mountain!

18:59.790 --> 19:01.840
Where's the horror movie?

19:01.840 --> 19:04.370
Sharks? On a snowy mountain?

19:15.620 --> 19:16.380
<i>Huh?</i>

19:16.380 --> 19:17.850
<i>What's that smell?</i>

19:21.940 --> 19:23.090
Here we go!

19:26.560 --> 19:27.740
Isaac.

19:29.420 --> 19:30.210
I—

19:30.210 --> 19:34.350
I think you ought to 
apologize to Philomela,

19:34.350 --> 19:37.310
whether she accepts your apology or not.

19:37.310 --> 19:42.580
Also, I'm not taking back what
 I said to you, nor am I apologizing.

19:43.180 --> 19:45.730
I honestly want you to change.

19:48.290 --> 19:49.300
All right.

19:49.780 --> 19:50.690
I'll be careful.

19:52.650 --> 19:54.550
Violet told me the same thing.

19:55.720 --> 19:57.380
Come on...

19:58.450 --> 20:02.460
<i>You basically just admitted you didn't
 take it to heart when I talked to you.</i>

20:04.610 --> 20:05.590
Nah.

20:05.590 --> 20:06.660
Never mind.

20:07.960 --> 20:09.600
<i>Seriously.</i>

20:09.600 --> 20:12.860
<i>You're so weirdly straightforward and dense.</i>

20:15.270 --> 20:17.850
Man, that was a hell of a way to waste time.

20:17.850 --> 20:19.840
Refreshingly bold plot, right?

20:19.840 --> 20:21.980
Even though everybody died a spectacular death?

20:21.980 --> 20:24.980
Well, aren't you all up quite late?

20:26.520 --> 20:30.270
Enjoy the watch party, everyone?

20:30.270 --> 20:33.410
We're escorting you naughty 
kids to the dorms.

20:33.410 --> 20:34.960
Okay.

20:44.470 --> 20:46.040
What's the matter?

20:46.040 --> 20:47.760
You seem down.

20:47.760 --> 20:49.240
It's nothing.

20:53.800 --> 20:55.130
Violet.

21:00.600 --> 21:03.840
Tonight was a lot of fun.

21:03.840 --> 21:05.360
I liked hanging out with everyone.

21:07.190 --> 21:08.380
Where'd that come from?

21:08.380 --> 21:09.910
What are we, strangers?

21:09.910 --> 21:11.520
Are we still doing something?

21:11.520 --> 21:12.610
Let's go to bed.

21:12.610 --> 21:15.130
I'm glad you had fun.

21:15.820 --> 21:18.340
Whoever you are.

21:31.420 --> 21:33.340
Come play with me again.

21:39.790 --> 21:41.440
The kimodameshi...

21:41.830 --> 21:43.450
...was a huge success.

21:44.650 --> 21:48.900
Well, what a skillful 
impostor that ghost was.

21:48.900 --> 21:52.700
That was a student from about 30 
years ago, if I recall correctly.

21:58.010 --> 22:00.720
Get off me, Kevin! You're heavy!

22:00.720 --> 22:02.090
Hold me!

22:00.770 --> 22:01.800
Chise.

22:02.090 --> 22:02.950
Don't leave me behind!

22:04.100 --> 22:06.960
Alexandra is asking you to 
come to the nurse's office.

22:11.010 --> 22:12.530
As quick as you can.
